{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261112T181133Z_dev-03_flat_8c69", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "In Kim, Lee, Park and Shin (arXiv:1601.05089), the best fit for annihilation dominated by ψψ̄ → h2h2 used m_ψ = 69.2 GeV and m_h2 = 35.7 GeV. The annihilation cross section is ⟨σv⟩ = 2.26×10^-26 cm^3 s^-1. The canonical J-factor was rescaled by 𝒥 = 2.2, so J̄ = 2.2 × J̄_canonical. This fit gives χ² = 23.19 (p-value 0.39). The paper's pure-pseudoscalar coupling (sinξ = 1) applies here. The newer paper (2610.26648v1) revisits this scenario but does not restate these numbers.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "7"}]}, "turns": 8, "seconds": 27.358, "tool_calls": 8, "tool_result_chars": 255216, "input_tokens": 730924, "output_tokens": 1169, "parser_versions": ["3"], "ended_at": "2026-11-12T18:12:01+00:00"}
